<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Hoechst yr headline shr slides, div up.</title>
<headline>Hoechst yr headline shr slides, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline	     23.4	 vs     41.3</p>
<p>    - attrib		 26.7	 vs     45.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 8.0	 vs     7.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	 40.98	 vs     66.78</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		 31.31	 vs     59.27</p>
<p>    Tax			1.72	 vs     9.18</p>
<p>    Finance costs	 38.20	 vs     40.29</p>
<p>    Turnover	   1,857.63	 vs     1,753.50</p>
<p>Div payable April 11</p>
<p>on register March 27</p>
<p>Full name: Hoechst South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     5.13	   vs    6.23</p>
<p>NOTE - A restructuring of Hoechst Noristan and the divestment of non-core activities during 1996 were reflected in the weak contribution from the pharmaceutical operation, the firm said.</p>
<p>It said benefits from the formation of Hoechst Marion Roussel, which will be one of the top three pharmaceutical companies in South Africa, will materialise in 1997 and the outlook for the business was positive.</p>
<p>Hoechst said, while mindful of the vagaries of worldwide fibre prices, it was confident of an improved performance in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
